This sample shows how to use the hitTest() method on the Map component to access features in a VectorTileLayer. This is done by setting up a pointer-move event handler on the Map component and passing the returned x, y screen coordinates to the hitTest() method, along with additional options to only include graphics from the VectorTileLayer. The method returns a promise, resolving to an array of objects containing any features retrieved from the VectorTileLayer. Subsequently, the content is generated to include contours information and is presented in a tooltip.

